# RULE: Interface Internationalization

Applies to renderer UI and UI-facing application logic.

## Mandatory

- Every UI or UI-facing logic change updates translation keys for **all** supported locales (`ru`, `en`, `fr`, `de`, `bg`).
- No hardcoded user-visible copy in renderer components, shells, hooks, UI helpers, icon labels, or application projections.
- Domain emits technical reason keys/events only; never localized sentences.
- Application projections prefer semantic message keys + interpolation params over localized text.
- Renderer resolves text via selected `UserSettings.language` and applies language immediately.
- Translation resources are allowed only in approved i18n modules and test/story fixtures.

## Validation

- Locale catalogs compile with key parity.
- `npm run i18n:check` passes.
- Tests cover translation keys or rendered localized text for touched modules.
- Feature Registry and `docs/softphone/I18N-Coverage.md` are updated for migration progress.
